A||||6||turbo86se||Found A-arm problem!||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||11-02-2001||01:09 PM||||I think I found why my F/R wheel sits inward, towards the top of the '88 Fiero. Going by my Haynes manual, there are two bolts that secure the pivot arm to the crossmember. The bolt to the right, has been forced about .5" inwards. I can clearly see that is has been moved, the metal has been scraped clean. <BR>In case you don't know, the F/R caliper came loose, two bolts were gone, and the caliper lodged into the wheel. You should see the inside of the wheel! Now I've got a new caliper installed, along with new shocks. The car pulled heavily to the right, and tracked real bad.<P>Any suggestions on how to fix this? Will I need new parts? Could I just reposition the pivot bar?<BR>Thanks!!!!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||KissMySSFiero||11-02-2001||01:38 PM||||Thats the alignment ajustment.  your camber and caster are going to be WAY OFF.  camber you can see,  thats why the wheel sits in so much.  Its also the reason the car pulls hard right.  you can either eyeball it and try to move it back to its original position.  then drive the car and see how she goes.  if all seems right i would still take it to a shop and get it checked out.  glad to see your back on the road.  <P>by the way do you have any pics of your black cars wheels. im looking for wheels for myself and i liked yours when i saw them but cant really remember what they look like.  TIA<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <BR>88FORMULA<BR>       <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>        <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||11-02-2001||01:58 PM||||Thanks JoeJoe!<BR>With the help of Ed Parks, I loosened the two bolts, and pulled the arm back into position. It kinda locked in where it was supposed to be. I got the bolts as tight as I could, and set her down.<BR>The wheel is straight! The steering wheel is straight! It drives awesome! I can take my hands off the wheel now! Oops watch the mail-lady! <BR>I'm still going to get it aligned, of course, and have them check my handy-work! I'm so happy I can drive my coupe again!!!!<P>JoeJoe I'll email you some pics, still can't figure out the PIP thing!<P>And thanks Pondski, skitime, Phil, DRH, Blackice, Galen for putting up with me and all my questions!||||reg||10
Z||000003||skitime||11-02-2001||03:00 PM||||Hey Turbo,  that happened to me when I first got my 88 t-top.  I was stopping and and heard a big bang in the front end.  After doing some checking I saw the upper A-arm had shifted.  Hmmm There must be a lot of weak allignment guys out there that can't tighten the bolts enough.  Glad you got it straightened out.  <P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-02-2001||07:58 PM||||For safety I strongly recomend replacing that wheel if you haven't already. It may have a slow crack started that could let go with no warning later. That's a hell of allot of impact to move a control arm like that.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||turbo86se||11-02-2001||09:14 PM||||Hmm, that's a good point. Thanks for bringing that to my attention. The inside of the wheel got scraped up pretty good, I didn't hit anything, just ran off onto some dirt and grass. I'll keep my eyes open for a new front wheel.<BR>Thanks theogre!||||reg||1
Z||000006||DRH||11-03-2001||12:20 AM||||Good to hear the alignment adjustment absorbed the impact. If it hadn't slipped it would probably have broken or bent something else.<P><BR>||||reg||14
